node_modules/
# dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is COMMITTED (v1.2): every consumer
# installs from a git tag, and a git install runs no lifecycle script, so a dist
# built only at publish time exists for nobody. `npm run check:build` fails if it
# is stale. Do not add `dist/` here.
# Both halves. Comparison is a byte-exact PNG match, so a baseline is valid only
# on the machine that recorded it — committing this box's set would make CI
# permanently red rather than green. CI must record its own inside its image.
.visual/
*.log
.DS_Store
# This repo's lockfile is `package-lock.json` — every script here is npm, and CI
# runs `npm install`. A `pnpm-lock.yaml` shows up whenever someone runs pnpm in
# this directory (the consumers are pnpm projects, and this tree sits beside
# them), and a second lockfile is worse than none: neither one is obviously the
# authority, and the two resolve the same range to different trees. Ignore it
# rather than commit it — if this repo ever moves to pnpm, that is a deliberate
# change that deletes the npm lockfile in the same commit.
pnpm-lock.yaml
